  #line-at(72.024pt, 83.18pt, "substrate curvature decreases the overall capillary force, owing to the reduced curvatures of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.82pt, "the liquid bridge, while the temporal evolution of the adhesion force is strongly influenced by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.58pt, "both substrate curvature and wettability. Our findings offer valuable insights towards design ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 145.22pt, "guidelines for evaporation-driven particle assembly, microgravity experiments, precise ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.98pt, "atomic force microscopy, bio-sensors design, additive manufacturing, and niche micro-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.62pt, "fabrication processes, where the dynamic evolution of liquid-bridge geometry and adhesion ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.38pt, "critically determines particle packing, structural integrity, and the consequent microstructure. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 236.06pt, "Keywords:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.98pt, 236.06pt, " capillary bridge, evaporation, substrate curvature, wettability, Marangoni flow, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 256.85pt, "Arbitrary Lagrangian-Eulerian (ALE).  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 312.77pt, "1.  Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 336.29pt, "Capillary bridges (or liquid bridges) often play fundamental roles in thermo-fluidic, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 356.93pt, "species transport phenomena between adjacent solid substrates. These structures are formed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 377.69pt, "when a small liquid-mass is partially stretched or squeezed between two solid substrates very ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 398.33pt, "close to one another, and are relevant to several natural and industrial processes. For instance, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 419.11pt, "the transient changes in mechanical properties of unsaturated soil, wet granular matter, and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 439.75pt, "porous media greatly depend on their liquid retention capability, which in turn is governed by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 460.39pt, "the evaporation behavior of liquid in the form of capillary bridges [1-3]. The hydrodynamics ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 481.15pt, "and deformation in seepage flow through unsaturated fractures (in geophysical flows, and oil ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 501.79pt, "recovery applications) greatly depend on formation of these bridges [4]. The formation, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 522.55pt, "stability, and evaporation of liquid bridges are relevant to several scientific application such ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.19pt, "as printing technology [5], trickle bed reactors [6], atomic force microscopy [7], microgravity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 563.95pt, "experiments [8], dispensing of glue in packaging, leather, rubber and vinyl industries [9], heat ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 584.62pt, "switch system in electronic cooling [10], and in micro-plating applications [11]. Also, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 605.38pt, "evaporating capillary bridges play a pivotal role in particle assembly and self-assembly by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 626.02pt, "generating capillary forces that drive particle rearrangement and organization into ordered ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 646.78pt, "micro- and nanostructures, thereby enabling fabrication of functional materials and coatings ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 667.42pt, "[12].")
  #line-at(99.264pt, 667.42pt, "Hence, an in-depth understanding of the interfacial profile evolution and thermo-fluid-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 688.18pt, "species transport behavior of capillary bridges during evaporation under varied circumstances ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 708.82pt, "is essential for the rational design and optimization of the aforementioned processes.")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 737.5pt, "Under mechanical equilibrium, the capillary profile is governed by Young-Laplace ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 759.24pt, "equation: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.568pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(142.134pt, 762.63pt, "0")
