  #line-at(469.54pt, 83.18pt, " coordinate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.82pt, "system, as shown schematically in fig. 1(a). The liquid bridge is formed between the curved ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 124.58pt, "faces of two adjacent cylindrical substrates possessing identical curvature, with the contact ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 145.22pt, "diameter being equal to the substrate diameter, as illustrated in Fig. 1(a, b). The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 165.98pt, "corresponding geometrical specifications at the interface (such as gorge radius and external ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 186.62pt, "radius of curvature) and at the contact line (such as contact angle, radius of curvature at solid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 207.38pt, "substrate) are illustrated in fig. 1(b). This configuration highlights the intrinsic influence of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 228.02pt, "substrate curvature on the internal thermo-fluid dynamics while minimizing its effect on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.81pt, "surrounding vapor concentration field. To investigate the role of curvature, the curvature ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 269.45pt, "magnitude of both the upper and lower substrates is varied over a wide range, as summarized ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 291.17pt, "in Table 1. For wettability effects, we consider the solid-liquid contact angle ")
  #line-at(452.86pt, 291.17pt, " = ")
  #line-at(473.14pt, 291.17pt, "/4 and ")
  #line-at(513.1pt, 291.17pt, " = ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 313.25pt, "5")
  #line-at(84.624pt, 313.25pt, "/6 representing hydrophilic and SH nature of the surfaces. Furthermore, aluminum (k = ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 334.25pt, "238 W/m.K), alumina (k = 27 W/m.K), glass (k = 1.4 W/m.K) and acrylic plastic (k = 0.18 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 355.01pt, "W/m.K) are selected as substrate materials to elucidate the influence of solid thermal ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 375.65pt, "conductivity relative to that of the liquid domain. For all cases, the initial volume (")
