  #line-at(72.024pt, 338.93pt, "value at the three-phase contact line to the lowest value at the neck region. As a result, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 359.69pt, "stable flow field consist of two counteracting vortices transferring fluid from the contact line ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.33pt, "towards neck region along interface.  In case of SH surfaces (see fig 7(a)), a more uniform ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 401.09pt, "mass flux cools the entire interface in a more even manner thereby lowering the liquid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 421.75pt, "domain temperature than the solid. As a result, the counter-rotating vortices become clearly ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.51pt, "discernible from the onset of evaporation and become increasingly pronounced upon reaching ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 463.15pt, "the stable state. ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 489.91pt, "Now, although this evaporation induced thermo-flow-field remain qualitatively ")
